---
/**
 * foodcraft / PageBP — "Tahanan Cafe · Split" (a neighbourhood cafe drawn as a
 * two-column page).
 *
 * THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION. Every value below is lifted verbatim from
 * "Tahanan Cafe Landing v4.dc.html". Nothing is re-derived, darkened or "made
 * portable".
 *
 * WHAT MAKES THIS ONE DIFFERENT FROM ITS SIBLING. foodcraft:BM is the same
 * cafe, and shares its white ground and its walnut, but it is a CONTAINED
 * page: everything sits inside a 1160px measure and the hairlines divide
 * content inside it. BP is a SPLIT page. Nine of its thirteen blocks are a
 * full-bleed 50/50 grid — copy on one half, a photograph running edge to edge
 * on the other — and the halves alternate down the page so the picture crosses
 * from right to left and back. The only container in the design is the four
 * blocks that have no photograph at all (Credentials, Service area, FAQ,
 * Footer). They are not the same template with different fonts; they are laid
 * out on different bones.
 *
 * THREE SIGNATURES, and none of them is the colour:
 *   1. THE FULL-BLEED SPLIT. `.split` is a grid of two equal tracks with a
 *      hairline down the middle and one under the whole section. The copy half
 *      carries the padding; the photo half carries none and bleeds to the
 *      viewport edge. A section that wraps its copy in `.wrap` has stopped
 *      being this design.
 *   2. THE ITALIC WALNUT CLOSE. Every headline turns italic and walnut for its
 *      last phrase — "Stay as long <em>as you like.</em>". DM Serif Display
 *      ships a real 400 italic, so this is drawn, not a synthesised oblique.
 *   3. THE HAIRLINE LEDGER. Facts, hours, menu rows, delivery areas and specs
 *      are all the same object: a baseline-aligned row with a hairline under
 *      it and its value pushed to the right edge. `.rowrule` is that object,
 *      and six sections draw with it.
 *
 * TOKEN NAMING IS CHECKED AGAINST THE ENGINE, NOT ASSUMED.
 * astro-site-template/src/lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts owns a fixed list of
 * token names and wins each with an important declaration. Every name below
 * was grepped against that file before use.
 *
 *   OWNED BY THE ENGINE, deliberately — these are the axes a scheme SHOULD
 *   move: --paper --card --ink --ink-soft --line --muted --accent
 *   --accent-deep --accent-rgb --ink-rgb --paper-rgb --on-ink --on-paper
 *   --on-accent --on-primary, and the four font tokens --disp --serif --sans
 *   --mono. Note --muted is remapped to palette.inkSoft, so the muted contrast
 *   figure below is this palette's NATIVE value and not a guarantee under
 *   every scheme.
 *
 *   INVISIBLE TO THE ENGINE, each verified absent from that file:
 *   --tint --well --line-2 --line-3 --line-tint --accent-2 --band --band-kick
 *   --band-body --on-band --on-cream --r --maxw --pad --pad-x. The band trio
 *   matters most:
 *   they were chosen against #231A13 specifically and must not move. The
 *   walnut itself is 2.41:1 on that ground, which is why the closing band's
 *   eyebrow is --band-kick and never --accent.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head, tokens, fonts,
 * Leaflet, skip link, scroll-reveal). It does NOT compose with BaseLayout. It
 * is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`; the 15 section
 * components receive `layout` + `content` and nothing else.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. It READS layout.businessName and
 * layout.tagline for the title, content.description, layout.favicon and
 * layout.ogImage. Every data-field lives in a section.
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING is the skip link's "Skip to content".
 *
 * ONE PLACEMENT DEVIATION, stated rather than hidden. The design nests its
 * TRUST cells INSIDE the hero's copy column, as a two-by-two ruled grid under
 * the buttons. This repo reads a template's toggleable sections off the lines
 * of THIS file — scripts/check-template-blocks.mjs fails any rendered section
 * that is not gated here — so a Trust nested inside HeroBP could never be
 * switched off by an owner. TrustBP therefore renders as its own gated section
 * immediately under the hero, four cells across on one ruled row. Every value
 * inside a cell is the design's: the serif walnut figure at 21px, the 12.5px
 * 500-weight label beside it, the hairline beneath. Only the placement moved.
 *
 * VERIFIED CONTRAST — COMPUTED from the hexes declared below (sRGB relative
 * luminance, WCAG 2.x), not estimated:
 *   ink/paper 17.09 · ink/tint 16.15 · ink/well 15.36
 *   ink-soft/paper 7.73 · ink-soft/tint 7.31 · muted/paper 6.13
 *   accent/paper 7.11 (kickers, links, prices) · paper on an accent fill 7.11
 *   accent-deep/paper 11.00 (link hover) · accent-2/paper 5.85 (the stars)
 *   band-kick/band 7.45 · band-body/band 10.70 · paper/band 17.09
 *   on-cream/paper 11.76 (the cream button's label on the dark band)
 *   Nothing this design sets as TEXT sits below AA.
 *
 * TWO UI-BOUNDARY PAIRS THAT FAIL, reported and deliberately NOT changed. The
 * outlined secondary button's border is --line-2 on --paper: 1.42:1, against
 * the 3.00 that WCAG 1.4.11 asks of a control boundary. The hairline rules are
 * --line at 1.21:1. Both are the design's own values, drawn on a page whose
 * whole character is the quietness of its rules, and both controls stay
 * identifiable by a label at 17.09:1. Raising --line-2 to #9A8879 would clear
 * the button at 3.05 as a one-value change whenever that is wanted.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES here: .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light
 * .nav-cta .nav-right .testi .cta-band .trust, and `.hero` on a section.
 * Buttons here are .btn--fill / .btn--line / .btn--paper / .btn--pale.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (wrapper-local): astro-builder defaults
 * layout.fontPairing to 'modern' and lockVariant only blanks
 * ''/'auto'/'default', so without this buildOverrideCss would force-swap
 * DM Serif Display + DM Sans with an important declaration on ~every real
 * site.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER, exactly as the design draws it once Trust is unnested:
 * Header, Hero, Trust, About, Services (the menu), Why, How, Gallery,
 * Testimonials, Credentials, Location (visit), Area, Faq, CtaBand, Footer.
 *
 * Leaflet: LOADS leaflet.css + leaflet.js and defines
 * window.__foodcraftBPInitMap. LocationBP calls that exact string. Keep
 * `el.innerHTML = ''` in the boot and keep id="map" literal.
 */
import HeaderBP from './header/HeaderBP.astro';
import HeroBP from './hero/HeroBP.astro';
import TrustBP from './trust/TrustBP.astro';
import AboutBP from './about/AboutBP.astro';
import ServicesBP from './services/ServicesBP.astro';
import WhyBP from './why/WhyBP.astro';
import HowBP from './how/HowBP.astro';
import GalleryBP from './gallery/GalleryBP.astro';
import TestimonialsBP from './testimonials/TestimonialsBP.astro';
import CredentialsBP from './credentials/CredentialsBP.astro';
import LocationBP from './location/LocationBP.astro';
import AreaBP from './area/AreaBP.astro';
import FaqBP from './faq/FaqBP.astro';
import CtaBandBP from './ctaBand/CtaBandBP.astro';
import FooterBP from './footer/FooterBP.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
const __pairing = (layout.fontPairing === 'modern' && !layout.fontPairingExplicit) ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__pairing);
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __pairing);
const __desc = (content as any).description || '';
const __favicon = layout.favicon || '';
const __og = layout.ogImage || layout.favicon || '';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en-PH" data-page="BP">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>{title}</title>
{__desc && <meta name="description" content={__desc} />}
<meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
{__desc && <meta property="og:description" content={__desc} />}
{__og && <meta property="og:image" content={__og} />}
{__favicon && <link rel="icon" href={__favicon} />}

<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,300;9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
{__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
<!-- Leaflet. BOTH tags are load-bearing: without the stylesheet the tiles
     render unpositioned, and without the script window.L never exists and
     LocationBP's drawn fallback map-face is all an owner ever sees.
     check-template-blocks.mjs fails that combination. -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />

<style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       Every selector is prefixed html[data-page="BP"]. An unscoped rule here
       reaches all 67 templates. (Never write a literal end-style-tag inside
       this block, comments included — it is an HTML raw-text element.)
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BP"] {
      /* ── the white world ────────────────────────────────────────────────
            --tint is the design's #FBF8F5 section wash (Why, Credentials,
            FAQ); --well is #F7F2EC, the ground a photograph sits on before it
            loads and the colour of every empty plate. */
      --paper: #FFFFFF;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --tint: #FBF8F5;
      --well: #F7F2EC;

      --ink: #231A13;
      --ink-soft: #5B5148;
      --muted: #6A6057;

      /* THREE weights of rule, and the difference is load-bearing. --line is
         the structural hairline that divides the splits and closes each
         section. --line-3 is one shade lighter and is the LEDGER rule, under a
         fact row or a menu row. --line-2 is the one you can actually see, and
         only two things use it: the outlined button's border and the step
         disc. */
      --line: #EFE8E1;
      --line-2: #E3D7CA;
      --line-3: #F3EDE6;
      /* A FOURTH rule, and it exists because the design draws one. On the
         #FBF8F5 wash --line all but vanishes, so the two sections that sit on
         that ground (Why, FAQ) use a hairline one step darker. It is the
         design's own #EAE1D8 and is used nowhere else. */
      --line-tint: #EAE1D8;

      /* ── the accent, the one token this design itself exposes as
            configurable (its own data-props seeds a colour picker at #7A4E2D),
            and so the one the engine is welcome to move. --accent-2 is the
            review stars and nothing else. */
      --accent: #7A4E2D;
      --accent-deep: #573418;
      --accent-2: #8A5A34;
      --accent-rgb: 122,78,45;

      /* ── the closing band. Invisible to the engine on purpose: these four
            were chosen against #231A13 and must not move. --accent on that
            ground is 2.41:1, so the band's eyebrow is --band-kick. */
      --band: #231A13;
      --band-kick: #C9A57C;
      --band-body: #D5CBC1;
      --on-band: #FFFFFF;
      /* The cream button's label on the dark band. The design writes #4A3320
         rather than the ink, and it is 11.76:1 on white. */
      --on-cream: #4A3320;

      /* ── engine vocabulary it also rewrites; declared so nothing inherits a
            blank, and used deliberately. */
      --ink-rgb: 35,26,19;
      --paper-rgb: 255,255,255;
      --on-ink: #FFFFFF;
      --on-paper: #231A13;
      --on-accent: #FFFFFF;
      --on-primary: #FFFFFF;

      /* ── type + metrics ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
            2px is the ONLY radius in this design. There is no pill and no soft
            edge anywhere. */
      --disp: "DM Serif Display", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "DM Serif Display", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --mono: "DM Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --r: 2px;
      /* The design's two measures: 1180px with a 30px gutter for the four
         contained blocks, and 44px of gutter inside a split's copy half. Both
         scale DOWN on narrow viewports and neither ever exceeds the design. */
      --maxw: 1180px;
      --pad: clamp(18px, 2.4vw, 30px);
      --pad-x: clamp(22px, 3.2vw, 44px);
    }

    html[data-page="BP"] *,
    html[data-page="BP"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BP"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BP"] { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-padding-top: 84px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BP"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BP"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.78;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    /* THE ANCHOR RESET IS :where()-WRAPPED, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING — it is not
       decoration and it is not optional.
         `html[data-page="BP"] a`         scores (0,1,2) — two type selectors.
         `html[data-page="BP"] :where(a)` scores (0,1,1) — :where() contributes 0.
       Every button and link primitive below is `:where(.btn--fill)` and friends,
       which also score (0,1,1). Written as a bare `a`, the reset OUTRANKS all of
       them, and since every control on this page is an anchor, `color: inherit`
       wins over `color: var(--on-accent)` — the walnut button gets an ink label
       instead of a white one, and the cream button on the dark band gets a WHITE
       one on white. Neither is a hover state or an edge case: it is every
       control, in every scheme, on first paint.
       At (0,1,1) the reset ties with the primitives instead, and the tie is
       broken by source order — so the reset must also stay ABOVE them in this
       block. It does. Move it below and the bug returns silently. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    html[data-page="BP"] ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
    /* DM Serif Display has ONE weight, 400. Asking for a bold synthesises a
       smear, so 400 is stated here and no heading anywhere raises it. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ink);
      letter-spacing: 0; line-height: 1.1; text-transform: none;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(p) { margin: 0 0 1em; }

    /* ── THE CONTAINER, for the four blocks that have no photograph. Design:
          max-width:1180px; margin:0 auto; padding:… 30px. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.wrap) {
      width: 100%; max-width: var(--maxw); margin-inline: auto;
      padding-inline: var(--pad);
    }

    /* ── THE SPLIT. The design's spine: two equal tracks, a hairline down the
          middle and one under the section. `> * + *` puts the vertical rule
          between the halves whichever way round they are, so a section that
          flips the photograph to the left gets it for free. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split) {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: stretch;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split) > * + * { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
    /* One half only — no photograph was supplied. The copy takes the measure
       its column actually has at the design's own width rather than running
       the full viewport. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split--solo) { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split__copy) {
      padding: clamp(48px, 6vw, 66px) var(--pad-x);
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center;
      min-width: 0;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split--solo) .split__copy { max-width: 620px; }
    /* The photograph half. No padding: it bleeds to the viewport edge, which
       is the whole point of the layout. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split__shot) {
      position: relative; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden;
      background-color: var(--well);
    }

    /* ── THE EYEBROW. 10px caps at .32em in walnut. Unlike its BM sibling this
          one carries NO rule under it — the design draws none. line-height is
          pinned so the eyebrow's own line box does not inflate under body's
          1.78 and push the headline further down than the design draws it. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.kick) {
      display: inline-block; line-height: 1.1;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .32em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent);
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.h2) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400;
      font-size: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 48px); line-height: 1.1;
      margin: .24em 0 .32em; color: var(--ink); max-width: none;
    }
    /* THE SIGNATURE. A real drawn italic in walnut, on both the owner's own em
       and the tail this template derives from their sentence. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.h2 em),
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.h2 .em),
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.em) { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.lede) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: clamp(15.5px, 1.5vw, 16.5px);
      line-height: 1.86; max-width: 50ch; margin: 0;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.body) {
      color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.78;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.mono) {
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.3;
    }
    /* Every numeral this design sets large: the trust figures, the menu
       prices, the roman step numerals. Serif, walnut, tabular so a column of
       prices lines up. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.fig) {
      font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: var(--accent);
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums lining-nums; line-height: 1;
    }

    /* ── THE LEDGER ROW. Six sections draw with this: a baseline-aligned pair
          with the value pushed right and a hairline underneath. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.rowrule) {
      display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px;
      padding: 11px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-3); min-width: 0;
    }

    /* ── BUTTONS. The design's four, all 12.5px/.14em/700 caps at a 2px
          corner. Text colours route through the contrast tokens so an admin
          colour pick cannot produce a label the same value as its fill. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn) {
      /* DECLARED, not left to chance — the same guard commit 46c7214 added to
         the four sibling wrappers. A button with no background of its own is
         filled by whatever rule lands last, and index.astro bundles every
         template's is:global CSS onto every page, so an unscoped
         `.btn { background: … }` from another family used to paint this
         family's outline controls. Every variant below sets its own fill; this
         is what a bare .btn actually gets. */
      background-color: transparent;
      /* line-height DECLARED: the design sets none on its buttons, so they
         render at the browser normal. Inheriting body's 1.78 inflates every
         control by ~7px. A label is one line; 1 is what a button wants. */
      line-height: 1;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: .5em;
      padding: 16px 28px; min-height: 48px;
      border-radius: var(--r); border: 1px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 12.5px;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
      text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background-color .18s ease, color .18s ease, border-color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--fill) { background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) { background-color: var(--accent-deep); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent-deep); }
    /* The outlined secondary. Its LABEL is the ink at 17.09:1; only its border
       is the quiet --line-2, which is the pair reported in the header
       comment. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--line) { background-color: transparent; color: var(--on-paper); border-color: var(--line-2); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--line:hover) { background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
    /* The two that live on the dark closing band. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--paper) { background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--on-cream); border-color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--paper:hover) { background-color: var(--band-kick); color: var(--on-cream); border-color: var(--band-kick); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--pale) { background-color: transparent; color: var(--on-band); border-color: rgba(var(--paper-rgb), .42); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn--pale:hover) { background-color: var(--on-band); color: var(--band); border-color: var(--on-band); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BP"] .btn { transition: none; } }

    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4em; min-height: 44px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent);
      transition: color .18s ease;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.linkc:hover) { color: var(--accent-deep); }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BP"] .linkc { transition: none; } }

    html[data-page="BP"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.band-dark) :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline-color: var(--band-kick);
    }

    /* ── THE PLATE. Every photograph in this design is a background-image on a
          cream ground, so a missing or slow image leaves the design's own
          #F7F2EC rather than a hole. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.plate) {
      position: relative; overflow: hidden; min-height: 180px;
      background-color: var(--well); isolation: isolate;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.plate) .ph {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1;
      background-color: var(--well);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      background-image:
        radial-gradient(78% 64% at 22% 14%, rgba(var(--accent-rgb), .10), transparent 62%),
        radial-gradient(66% 60% at 84% 90%, rgba(var(--ink-rgb), .05), transparent 60%);
      transition: transform .5s ease;
    }
    /* The gallery caption chip. An OPAQUE paper tile carrying the ink at
       17.09:1, so it holds over any photograph an owner uploads. */
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.plate) .cap {
      position: absolute; left: 12px; bottom: 12px; z-index: 3;
      max-width: calc(100% - 24px);
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--on-paper);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 9.5px;
      letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 6px 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BP"] :where(.plate) .ph { transition: none; } }

    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.band-dark) { background-color: var(--band); color: var(--on-band); }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.band-tint) { background-color: var(--tint); }

    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.reveal) { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); transition: opacity .6s ease, transform .6s ease; }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.reveal.in) { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="1"]) { transition-delay: .08s; }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="2"]) { transition-delay: .16s; }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.reveal[data-delay="3"]) { transition-delay: .24s; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html[data-page="BP"] .reveal { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    }

    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent);
      padding: 12px 18px; font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px;
    }
    html[data-page="BP"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }

    /* ── THE COLLAPSE. Below 900px the two halves stack, and the vertical
          hairline between them becomes a horizontal one. Every split section
          gets this at once, so no section has to restate it. */
    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split) { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split) > * + * { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.split--solo) .split__copy { max-width: none; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 760px) {
      /* The MAX is 27px, pinned just UNDER the base clamp's value where this
         query takes over: 3.6vw is 27.4px at 761px, so the step across the
         boundary runs DOWNWARD. Anything higher and the headline GROWS as the
         viewport narrows past 761 — a jump no screenshot at 1440 or 375 can
         show you, because it lives in the one pixel either side. */
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.h2) { font-size: clamp(25px, 6.6vw, 27px); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.lede) { max-width: none; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 520px) {
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.kick) { font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: .24em; }
      html[data-page="BP"] :where(.btn) { padding: 15px 22px; }
    }
</style>

<style is:inline set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
{visibility.headerSection !== false && <HeaderBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
<main id="main">
  {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBP content={content} layout={layout} />}
</main>
{visibility.footerSection !== false && <FooterBP content={content} layout={layout} />}

<script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    var els = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
    if (!els.length) return;
    if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) ||
        window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
      els.forEach(function (el) { el.classList.add('in'); });
      return;
    }
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      entries.forEach(function (e) {
        if (e.isIntersecting) { e.target.classList.add('in'); io.unobserve(e.target); }
      });
    }, { rootMargin: '0px 0px -8% 0px', threshold: 0.06 });
    els.forEach(function (el) { io.observe(el); });
  })();

  window.__foodcraftBPInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
    var tries = 0;
    (function go() {
      var el = document.getElementById('map');
      if (!el) return;
      if (typeof window.L === 'undefined') { if (tries++ < 25) setTimeout(go, 80); return; }
      el.innerHTML = '';
      var map = window.L.map(el, { scrollWheelZoom: false, attributionControl: true }).setView([lat, lng], 16);
      window.L.tileLayer('https://{s}.basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
        maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd', attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO',
      }).addTo(map);
      var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
      var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#7A4E2D';
      var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#FFFFFF';
      var icon = window.L.divIcon({
        className: '', iconSize: [16, 16], iconAnchor: [8, 8],
        html: '<span style="display:block;width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:' +
              accent + ';border:3px solid ' + paper + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 1px ' + accent + '"></span>',
      });
      var marker = window.L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon }).addTo(map);
      if (label) marker.bindPopup(label);
    })();
  };
</script>
</body>
</html>
